# DevOps Task

## Overview
This Task demonstrates a version-controlled DevOps workflow using Git and GitHub. It covers repository initialization, meaningful commits, branch management, pull requests, merge conflict handling, `.gitignore`, Git tags, and Markdown documentation.

## Objectives
- Maintain Task history with Git.
- Use `main`, `dev`, and feature branches.
- Integrate changes through GitHub Pull Requests.
- Keep generated files and secrets out of version control.
- Mark a stable project version using a Git tag.

